     Maybe somebody could tell me if this is supposed to happen:

I have played at least 5 games in which I got to the castle, and, lo
and behold, there was no wand of wishing. I am certain that on at least
one of these occasions a gelatinous cube ate the wand before I could get
to it, but I am equally certain that there was no g. cube present at least
two other times to eat the wand.  I killed literally everthing in the castle
and first level of hell (on the assumption that some monster had picked up
the wand and possibly fallen through the trapdoors), searched all corpses and
came up with nothing.
   Needless to say, this really sucked...well, 5 times.  Since I have only
made it to the castle around 10 times, I've had a 50% miss ratio for that
damn w.o.w.  I have even quaffed a potion of object detection immediately
upon getting to the castle level and not spotted the wand.  Although
I managed to finish the game once without the wand, I had to polypile a lot
to get some decent items.  The dungeons can be very dry of scrolls, potions
and other useful things.
   I do not subscribe to the belief that anyone who can finish the castle
level can finish that game, regardless of whether the wand was there or not,
and I think that the code should be fixed to prevent the w.o.w. from not
being there or even disappearing somehow.  It is an important part of the
game, and in a sense it's the only good thing you always have to look
forward to.  Anyone who's made it all the way to the castle with a miserable
wimp of an archeologist or tourist, and been robbed of the wand somehow,
should feel justly cheated--the game is hard enough without knocks like
that.


